{ In this position the power of the Rook is demonstrated by the first move, }
1. Ra7 { , which immediately confines the Black King to the last rank, and the mate is quickly accomplished by: } 1... Kg8 2. Kg2 { . The combined action of King and Rook is needed to arrive at a position in which mate can be forced. The general principal for a beginner to follow is to keep his King as much as possible on the same rank, or file, as the opposing King. } 2... Kf8 3. Kf3 Ke8 4. Ke4 Kd8 5. Kd5 Kc8 { When, in this case, the King has been brought to the sixth rank, it is better to place it, not on the same file, but on the one next to it towards the center. } 6. Kd6 (6. Kc6? { the Black King will go back to } 6... Kd8 { and it will take much longer to mate. }) 6... Kb8 { If now the King moves back to d8, Ra8 mates at once. } (6... Kd8 7. Ra8#) 7. Rc7 Ka8 8. Kc6 Kb8 9. Kb6 Ka8 10. Rc8# *


