1. Bd3 Kg8 2. Bg5 Kf7 3. Bf5 { and already the Black King is confined to a few squares.
We might now continue: } 3... Kg7 4. Kf2 Kf7 5. Kg3 Kg7 6. Kh4 Kf7 7. Kh5 Kg7 8. Bg6 Kg8 9. Kh6 Kf8 { White must now move one of the Bishops, so as to force the Black King to go back: } 10. Bh5 Kg8 11. Be7 Kh8 { Now the White Bishop must take up a position from which it can give check next move along the White diagonal, when the Black King moves back to g8. } 12. Bg4 Kg8 13. Be6+ Kh8 14. Bf6# *


