{ The example given should be sufficient proof. We give a few moves of the main variation: }
1. a4 a5 2. Kg2! { (Best; see why.) } 2... Kf4 3. b4! { (Best.) } 3... axb4 4. a5 b3 5. a6 b2 6. a7 b1=Q 7. a8=Q Qe4+ 8. Qxe4+ Kxe4 { This brings the game to a position which is won by Black, and which constitutes one of the classical endings of King and Pawns. I shall try to explain the guiding idea of it to those not familiar with it. } *


