{ Suppose in the starting position White plays }
1. Kd4 { Now Black has the option of either opposing the passage of the White King by playing } (1. Kf3 Kd5 { this form is the close diagonal opposition }) (1. Kf4 Kd5 2. Kf5 { this form is the 'close lateral' opposition. }) 1... Kd6 { or, if he prefers, he can pass with his own King by replying: } (1... Kf5) *


