{ The best move is: }
1. Qg5+ (1. Qe5+? Kf8 2. Kg6 Rd7 { The only defense, but, unfortunately, a very effective one, which makes it very difficult for White, since he cannot play } 3. Qe6 { because of } 3... Rg7+ 4. Kf6 Rg6+ { draws. }) 1... Kh8 (1... Kh7 2. Qg6+ Kh8 3. Kh6!) (1... Kf8 2. Qd8+ Kg7 3. Kg5 Rf3 4. Qd4+ Kf8 5. Kg6 { 5 Qd6+ Kg7; 6 Qe5+, Kf8; 7 Kg6 would also win the Rook. The text move, however, is given to show the finesse of such endings. White now threatens mate at d8. }) 2. Qe5+ Kh7 3. Kg5 Ra7! 4. Qe4+ Kg8 5. Qc4+ Kh7 6. Kf6 Rg7 7. Qh4+ Kg8 8. Qh5 { and we have the position of Example 40 with Black to move. } *


